PART 2 — THE RECONSTRUCTED ENGINE FUNCTION
(the reconstructed portion of doc_viewer/doc_viewer.c)

The doc_viewer mod works by replacing one engine function with a modified copy of it. The
reconstructed function body it carries is, by nature, a derivative representation of the design
and behavior of the engine of the 1996 game "Realms of the Haunting", produced by studying the
game's original executable. It is not covered by the MIT grant above.

That reconstructed portion is provided under the same preservation-notice terms as the
reconstructed engine in the ROTH.C repository — published for the purposes of preservation,
study, and interoperability, in the spirit of long-standing community practice around the
preservation of historical software. See the "reconstructed engine" part of the LICENSE file in
the ROTH.C engine repository for the full terms:

  https://github.com/beyond-the-ire/ROTH.C

The copyright in the underlying game and its program remains with its rights holders; nothing
here grants, transfers, or diminishes any of their rights. No game assets are included. To play
the game you must own it. If you are a rights holder of "Realms of the Haunting" and have
concerns, please open an issue; concerns will be addressed promptly and in good faith.


"Realms of the Haunting" and associated marks are the property of their respective owners. This
project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the game's developers, publishers,
or rights holders.
